Let MC_DATADIR relocate the data directory, and add MC_SYSCONFDIR.

mc keeps two installed trees apart: share_data_dir (share/mc - skins, syntax,
help, charsets) and sysconfig_dir (etc/mc - keymaps, mc.ext.ini, menus). Only
one of them could be moved, and it was the wrong one: MC_DATADIR was applied
to sysconfig_dir, leaving share_data_dir pinned to the compiled-in DATADIR.

So an archive unpacked outside its configured prefix found its skins, which
are searched under sysconfig_dir, but not the syntax files, which are not:

  Cannot open file /Users/<user>/.local/share/mc/syntax/Syntax

mc's manual already describes the intended behaviour - of MC_DATADIR it says
"If it's set, its value is used instead of %pkgdatadir% in the paths below",
%pkgdatadir% being share/mc. Make MC_DATADIR override share_data_dir as
documented, and give sysconfig_dir its own MC_SYSCONFDIR, so a relocated
install can point each at the right place. Both fall back to the values
compiled in at configure time.

--- a/src/main.c
+++ b/src/main.c
@@ -134,18 +134,25 @@
 OS_Setup (void)
 {
     const char *datadir_env;
+    const char *sysconfdir_env;
 
     mc_shell_init ();
 
-    /* This is the directory, where MC was installed, on Unix this is DATADIR */
+    /* This is the directory, where MC was installed, on Unix this is SYSCONFDIR */
+    /* and can be overridden by the MC_SYSCONFDIR environment variable */
+    sysconfdir_env = g_getenv ("MC_SYSCONFDIR");
+    if (sysconfdir_env != NULL)
+        mc_global.sysconfig_dir = g_strdup (sysconfdir_env);
+    else
+        mc_global.sysconfig_dir = g_strdup (SYSCONFDIR);
+
+    /* The package data directory, on Unix this is DATADIR */
     /* and can be overridden by the MC_DATADIR environment variable */
     datadir_env = g_getenv ("MC_DATADIR");
     if (datadir_env != NULL)
-        mc_global.sysconfig_dir = g_strdup (datadir_env);
+        mc_global.share_data_dir = g_strdup (datadir_env);
     else
-        mc_global.sysconfig_dir = g_strdup (SYSCONFDIR);
-
-    mc_global.share_data_dir = g_strdup (DATADIR);
+        mc_global.share_data_dir = g_strdup (DATADIR);
 }
 
